{"assets":["/statement-assets/d4851c80109b3b2bf000316871e9fd1e1b59282392e3d7faa503f617436a036f.png","/statement-assets/3de81c4e4e714dc9e6c4ce2ab7299020b5b513d4727ae1b1c77ae47a2b331f7f.png","/statement-assets/e5fc05dd9ecd4b240d2775006435c3d7cd2d5878a95526490043606f6597ee0b.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1017","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G. The Tree"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Abendsen assigned a mission to Juliana. In this mission, Juliana has a rooted tree with $$$n$$$ vertices. Vertex number $$$1$$$ is the root of this tree. Each vertex can be either black or white. At first, all vertices are white. Juliana is asked to process $$$q$$$ queries. Each query is one of three types:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If vertex $$$v$$$ is white, mark it as black; otherwise, perform this operation on all direct sons of $$$v$$$ instead. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Mark all vertices in the subtree of $$$v$$$ (including $$$v$$$) as white. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Find the color of the $$$i$$$-th vertex. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/d4851c80109b3b2bf000316871e9fd1e1b59282392e3d7faa503f617436a036f.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An example of operation \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (corresponds to the first example test). The vertices $$$1$$$ and $$$2$$$ are already black, so the operation goes to their sons instead."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Can you help Juliana to process all these queries?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$q$$$ ($$$2\\leq n\\leq 10^5$$$, $$$1\\leq q\\leq 10^5$$$) — the number of vertices and the number of queries."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n-1$$$ integers $$$p_2, p_3, \\ldots, p_n$$$ ($$$1\\leq p_i \\lt i$$$), where $$$p_i$$$ means that there is an edge between vertices $$$i$$$ and $$$p_i$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next $$$q$$$ lines contains two integers $$$t_i$$$ and $$$v_i$$$ ($$$1\\leq t_i\\leq 3$$$, $$$1\\leq v_i\\leq n$$$) — the type of the $$$i$$$-th query and the vertex of the $$$i$$$-th query."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the given graph is a tree."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each query of type $$$3$$$, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"black"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if the vertex is black; otherwise, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"white"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8 10\n1 2 1 2 5 4 5\n1 2\n3 2\n3 1\n1 1\n1 1\n3 5\n3 7\n3 4\n2 2\n3 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"black\nwhite\nblack\nwhite\nblack\nwhite\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8 11\n1 1 2 3 3 6 6\n1 1\n1 1\n1 3\n3 2\n3 4\n3 6\n3 7\n2 3\n1 6\n3 7\n3 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"black\nwhite\nblack\nwhite\nwhite\nblack\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first example is shown on the picture below."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/3de81c4e4e714dc9e6c4ce2ab7299020b5b513d4727ae1b1c77ae47a2b331f7f.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second example is shown on the picture below."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/e5fc05dd9ecd4b240d2775006435c3d7cd2d5878a95526490043606f6597ee0b.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"G","problemCode":"1017G","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1017/problem/G"}